 constrain-racial-progress\nDate/time: \n\n Tuesday 24 November 2026 \n\n 1
 :00pm to 2:00pm\n\n Location: \n\n Faculty of Law\, B16\n\n About \n\n Spe
 aker : Professor Atinuke Adediran (Associate Professor of Law\, Fordham Un
 iversity School of Law\, USA)\n Abstract :  Corporate law commonly treats
  disclosure as a means of providing information to investors and sharehold
 ers. This seminar asks what disclosure does when corporations speak about 
 racial inequality. Drawing on Disclosureland's original empirical study of
  statements\, pledges\, and regulatory filings from more than 2\,000 compa
 nies\, the book shows that corporate words operate as tools of governance\
 , shaping what firms recognize\, measure\, fund as philanthropic endeavors
 \, and ultimately choose to withdraw. Focusing on the proliferation of cor
 porate racial-equity commitments after 2020 and their subsequent softening
 \, narrowing\, or disappearance\, the seminar will identify three r
END:VEVENT
