 tute of Criminology\nTopics: Law\, Rights & Justice\, Criminology\nDetails
 : https://talks.cam.ac.uk/talk/index/273143/\nThis event is part of the In
 stitute of Criminology's Public Guest Seminar Series for Michaelmas Term 2
 026. A drinks reception follows the talk. These events are free and everyo
 ne is welcome. Please register to attend either in-person or online by cli
 cking the link at the bottom of this page. \n About What might it mean to 
 live a flourishing life? And what is the relationship between flourishing 
 and the virtues\, especially justice? In this talk based on her recent boo
 k\, Professor Angie Hobbs explores how Plato can help us with these urgent
  questions\, and how he addresses the key issue of character formation\, a
 nd why it never benefits us to return wrong for wrong. She shows how she h
 as used his methodology\, ideas and arguments in a variety of sectors to a
 ddress contemporary issues in education\, faith–secular debate\, health 
 care and the civil service\, and invites the audience to discuss with
END:VEVENT
